## 📖 About The Project

**Terra Twin AI** is an AI-powered virtual replica (Digital Twin) of Planet Earth. A "Digital Twin" is a virtual model of a physical entity that is updated with real-time data and used to simulate, predict, and optimize its behavior.

This project simulates the complex systems of our planet to forecast future scenarios. It allows users to interact with planetary data, visualize trends, and ask natural language questions to an AI (Gemini) to generate predictions.

> **Note:** This is a practice/educational project designed to demonstrate full-stack architecture, API integration, domain-driven design, and modern UI/UX. It uses simulated datasets and is **not** intended for production, enterprise, or real-world decision-making.

---

## 🌐 The 5 Prediction Domains

The digital twin is divided into 5 core modules, each tracking specific planetary indicators:

| Domain | Icon | Tracked Indicators | Example Prediction Query |
|--------|------|--------------------|--------------------------|
| **Environmental** | 🌡️ | Temperature, CO₂ levels, Air Quality Index (AQI), Deforestation rates, Sea-level rise | *"What will be the CO₂ level in 2030 if current trends continue?"* |
| **Economic** | 💰 | GDP growth, Inflation rates, Unemployment, Market trends, Currency fluctuations | *"Predict India's GDP growth for the next 5 years."* |
| **Industrial** | 🏭 | Manufacturing output, Energy consumption, Renewable energy adoption, Waste generation | *"How will industrial energy consumption change by 2040?"* |
| **Transportation** | 🚗 | Traffic density, EV adoption rates, Public transit usage, Carbon emissions from vehicles | *"What is the projected EV adoption rate in urban areas by 2035?"* |
| **Social** | 👥 | Population growth, Migration patterns, Healthcare access, Literacy rates, Urbanization | *"How will urban migration impact population density in 2050?"* |

---

## 🏗️ System Architecture

The project follows a modern, decoupled client-server architecture:

```text
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        CLIENT (React)                       │
│  - Vite + React 18                                          │
│  - Tailwind CSS (Dark Space Theme)                          │
│  - Recharts (Data Visualization)                            │
│  - react-globe.gl (3D Earth)                                │
└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘
                           │ HTTP Requests (Axios)
                           ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                      BACKEND (FastAPI)                      │
│  - Python 3.10+                                             │
│  - REST APIs (CRUD + Predictions)                           │
│  - JWT Authentication (OAuth2)                              │
│  - SQLAlchemy ORM                                           │
└─────────────┬──────────────────────────────┬────────────────┘
              │                              │
              ▼                              ▼
┌───────────────────────────┐  ┌──────────────────────────────┐
│     DATABASE (SQLite)     │  │      AI ENGINE (Gemini)      │
│  - Users                  │  │  - Google Generative AI API  │
│  - Environmental Data     │  │  - Model: gemini-1.5-flash   │
│  - Economic Data          │  │  - Natural Language to       │
│  - Prediction History     │  │    Forecasting               │
└───────────────────────────┘  └──────────────────────────────┘
⚙️ How It Works (Data Flow)
Data Generation (Simulation): Since we don't have real-time IoT sensors, the backend uses a Simulation Service to generate realistic, randomized time-series data for the 5 domains and seeds it into the database.

User Interaction: The user logs into the React dashboard and views interactive charts (Line, Bar, Area) representing the current planetary state.

Prediction Request: The user enters a query in the Prediction Dashboard (e.g., "Predict CO2 levels for the next 10 years").

Backend Processing:

The FastAPI backend receives the request.

It fetches the last 5 years of relevant historical data from SQLite.

It constructs a highly detailed prompt combining the user's question and the historical context.

Gemini AI Engine: The prompt is sent to the Gemini API. Gemini analyzes the historical context and returns a structured JSON forecast.

Storage & Visualization: The backend saves this prediction to the PredictionHistory table and sends it back to the frontend, where it is rendered as a beautiful chart.

🤖 Gemini AI Integration (Prompt Engineering)
The core magic lies in the gemini_service.py. We don't just ask Gemini random questions; we use Context-Aware Prompting.

Example Prompt Sent to Gemini:

"You are an expert environmental data scientist. Based on the following historical data for the past 5 years: [Data: 2020=400ppm, 2021=412ppm, 2022=418ppm...]. Predict the CO₂ levels for the next 5 years. Provide the output strictly in the following JSON format: {"year": 2025, "value": 425, "confidence": "High", "reasoning": "..."}."

This ensures the AI returns structured data that the frontend can easily plot on a chart, rather than just conversational text.

✨ Key Features
🌐 Interactive Earth Globe — Real-time visualization of planetary data on a 3D rotating globe.

📊 5 Domain Dashboards — Dedicated analytical views for Environment, Economy, Industry, Transport, and Society.

🤖 Gemini AI Predictions — Ask natural language questions and get AI-generated forecasts with reasoning.

📈 Rich Data Visualization — Line, Bar, Pie, Area, and Radar charts using Recharts.

🕓 Prediction History — Every forecast is stored securely and is easily revisitable.

🎨 Premium UI — Dark space theme with glassmorphism, smooth animations (Framer Motion), and fully responsive layout.

🔐 JWT Authentication — Secure Login and Register system with hashed passwords.

📚 Auto API Docs — Swagger UI available at /docs for easy testing.

